WEBVTT

00:00:00.213 --> 00:00:02.480
In Chennai, emergency calls, hospital

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:03.933
telemetry and payments rely on connected

00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:04.393
networks.

00:00:05.053 --> 00:00:07.073
When satellite backhaul fails, ORCA asks:

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.187
what happened, is recovery safe, and

00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:09.927
who needs to know?

00:00:10.852 --> 00:00:12.745
ORCA coordinates secure self-healing for

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:14.612
non-terrestrial networks, connecting cyber

00:00:14.612 --> 00:00:16.305
detection, incident response and policy

00:00:16.305 --> 00:00:16.645
review.

00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:17.992
Everything shown is emulated.

00:00:18.479 --> 00:00:20.065
This walkthrough uses deterministic mock

00:00:20.065 --> 00:00:22.085
agents, without live Qwen inference.

00:00:23.075 --> 00:00:24.508
Follow the complete flow.

00:00:25.208 --> 00:00:26.368
Six Chennai sites release telemetry

00:00:26.368 --> 00:00:26.961
progressively.

00:00:27.928 --> 00:00:29.461
Configuration scans and thirty-six features

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:32.208
feed four models: anomaly detection, minute

00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:34.635
forecasts, fault-or-attack assessment, and

00:00:34.635 --> 00:00:35.388
capacity allocation.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.130
Typed facts enter deterministic policy rules.

00:00:39.697 --> 00:00:41.190
Verified records support six possible

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:41.877
verdicts.

00:00:42.163 --> 00:00:44.043
Agents retrieve broader evidence and explain

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:44.530
proposals.

00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:47.313
An uncertain classifier can abstain; missing

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.477
facts remain visible.

00:00:49.602 --> 00:00:51.275
The commander reviews a scoped plan.

00:00:51.602 --> 00:00:53.989
Execution checks ownership, expiry, a cloned

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:54.982
test and path integrity.

00:00:55.415 --> 00:00:56.849
Staged changes receive health checks.

00:00:57.495 --> 00:00:58.989
Audit evidence and policy gaps follow

00:00:58.989 --> 00:00:59.942
separate review paths.

00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:03.315
Choose S1: the night Chennai’s satellite

00:01:03.315 --> 00:01:04.081
terminals disappear.

00:01:04.541 --> 00:01:05.115
Park Town and T.

00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:05.868
Nagar are affected.

00:01:06.448 --> 00:01:07.715
We follow one recording through released

00:01:07.715 --> 00:01:09.241
observations, commander decisions,

00:01:09.595 --> 00:01:11.095
containment, recovery and audit.

00:01:12.019 --> 00:01:13.559
The scenario launches a management intrusion.

00:01:14.045 --> 00:01:15.312
Stolen access enables destructive commands

00:01:15.312 --> 00:01:16.265
against emulated terminals.

00:01:16.779 --> 00:01:17.685
The target is the operator’s ground

00:01:17.685 --> 00:01:18.465
management network.

00:01:19.032 --> 00:01:19.979
Director truth stays separate from defending

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:20.935
agents’ observations.

00:01:22.213 --> 00:01:23.640
This run detects a management-plane attack

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.087
after two simulated minutes.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.093
M1 flags anomalies; M3 assesses the

00:01:28.093 --> 00:01:28.393
cause.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.547
Its uncalibrated model score is not

00:01:30.547 --> 00:01:31.420
a guaranteed probability.

00:01:32.519 --> 00:01:34.659
M2 forecasts link and battery risk,

00:01:34.692 --> 00:01:35.192
with uncertainty.

00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:37.339
M4 allocates scarce capacity.

00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:39.692
After recovery, this panel reports no

00:01:39.692 --> 00:01:40.712
reallocation needed.

00:01:41.079 --> 00:01:42.865
Model outputs inform decisions; they never

00:01:42.865 --> 00:01:43.672
authorise execution.

00:01:44.797 --> 00:01:46.343
Mobile and satellite operators own different

00:01:46.343 --> 00:01:46.977
responses.

00:01:47.463 --> 00:01:48.910
Supporting roles cover power, CERT,

00:01:49.143 --> 00:01:50.537
regulation, policy and gaps.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.383
Cited mock explanations expose available

00:01:52.383 --> 00:01:52.963
evidence.

00:01:53.277 --> 00:01:54.637
Roles without observations remain visibly

00:01:54.637 --> 00:01:55.083
inactive.

00:01:56.158 --> 00:01:57.778
First, contain the exposed account.

00:01:58.291 --> 00:01:59.871
Review its owner, target, clone test,

00:02:00.131 --> 00:02:01.111
risk and approval window.

00:02:01.451 --> 00:02:03.175
We demonstrate the commander controls: approve

00:02:03.175 --> 00:02:04.865
the exact plan, then inspect the

00:02:04.865 --> 00:02:05.471
guarded execution.

00:02:06.547 --> 00:02:07.720
Credential rotation and multi-factor

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.413
authentication require a separate hardening

00:02:09.413 --> 00:02:09.713
approval.

00:02:10.027 --> 00:02:11.533
The execution record shows five, twenty-five

00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:12.687
and one-hundred-percent health checks,

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.340
followed by blocked re-attack tests.

00:02:15.297 --> 00:02:17.043
Competing isolation and failover proposals

00:02:17.043 --> 00:02:18.183
raise a cited conflict.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.303
Segment isolation remains unexecuted.

00:02:20.763 --> 00:02:22.150
Our demonstrated sequence contains access

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.210
first, then authorises a verified backup.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:25.810
The conflict remains visible for review.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.280
Policy intelligence preserves distinct

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.493
reporting triggers: noticing, awareness and

00:02:30.493 --> 00:02:30.927
occurrence.

00:02:31.293 --> 00:02:32.827
Applicability depends on the entity and

00:02:32.827 --> 00:02:33.153
evidence.

00:02:33.533 --> 00:02:35.453
ORCA records clock ambiguity instead of

00:02:35.453 --> 00:02:37.033
hiding it inside one generated answer.

00:02:37.935 --> 00:02:38.002
Who warns dependent services?

00:02:38.002 --> 00:02:41.229
The warning-duty finding includes checked

00:02:41.229 --> 00:02:43.175
records, qualifications and international

00:02:43.175 --> 00:02:43.782
comparisons.

00:02:44.442 --> 00:02:45.815
A bounded search cannot prove that

00:02:45.815 --> 00:02:46.529
no rule exists.

00:02:47.269 --> 00:02:48.249
Humans review the gap and recommendation.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.022
The knowledge base distinguishes binding

00:02:51.022 --> 00:02:52.855
records, advisory guidance and drafts.

00:02:53.649 --> 00:02:54.929
This verified source calls the space

00:02:54.929 --> 00:02:55.762
framework advisory.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.535
Retrieval assists explanations.

00:02:58.462 --> 00:02:59.795
The fine-tuned Qwen model is a

00:02:59.795 --> 00:03:00.789
separate endpoint option.

00:03:01.713 --> 00:03:03.597
Review the domestic backup proposal: both

00:03:03.597 --> 00:03:05.793
target sites, owner, clone test and

00:03:05.793 --> 00:03:06.080
scope.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.013
Checks cover gateway location, integrity,

00:03:08.273 --> 00:03:09.800
availability and management containment.

00:03:10.233 --> 00:03:11.820
Approval still depends on backend execution

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:12.267
guards.

00:03:13.297 --> 00:03:14.937
Measured demand coverage returns at simulated

00:03:14.937 --> 00:03:16.023
minute fifty-seven.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.057
The degraded interval lasts thirty-three

00:03:18.057 --> 00:03:18.370
minutes.

00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:20.643
These sandbox timings reflect this stepped

00:03:20.643 --> 00:03:22.550
exercise and approvals, not real-world

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.263
recovery guarantees.

00:03:24.325 --> 00:03:25.525
Both sites change from path A

00:03:25.525 --> 00:03:26.545
to domestic backup B.

00:03:26.911 --> 00:03:28.285
Health checks pass and re-attack results

00:03:28.285 --> 00:03:28.758
are blocked.

00:03:29.378 --> 00:03:31.178
No rollback occurs here; unavailable

00:03:31.178 --> 00:03:33.078
validation is not presented as success.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.067
CERT and regulator roles receive emulated

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:36.847
bus notifications.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.080
Three scenario reporting windows record timely

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.960
notice; two earlier clock entries remain

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:41.327
open.

00:03:41.813 --> 00:03:43.473
No message reaches a real agency.

00:03:44.491 --> 00:03:45.611
Open the same recording in Audit

00:03:45.611 --> 00:03:45.965
and Replay.

00:03:46.505 --> 00:03:48.378
Filter rules, agents, approvals and execution.

00:03:49.025 --> 00:03:49.845
Inspect actors and evidence.

00:03:50.345 --> 00:03:51.765
The original hash chain verifies integrity,

00:03:52.105 --> 00:03:52.951
not every claim’s truth.

00:03:53.852 --> 00:03:55.492
This event records the exact failover

00:03:55.492 --> 00:03:55.819
approval.

00:03:56.105 --> 00:03:57.485
Replay stays read-only.

00:03:57.719 --> 00:03:59.665
Exports support review; the original recording

00:03:59.665 --> 00:04:00.912
retains chain verification.

00:04:01.479 --> 00:04:03.775
AI explains evidence and proposals; humans

00:04:03.775 --> 00:04:05.179
remain accountable for final judgement.

00:04:06.158 --> 00:04:08.441
Ten exercises cover normal operation, faults

00:04:08.441 --> 00:04:09.405
and cyber incidents.

00:04:09.985 --> 00:04:12.265
Additional injectors include GNSS and

00:04:12.265 --> 00:04:12.925
signalling attacks.

00:04:13.465 --> 00:04:14.605
Training includes synthetic data.

00:04:14.891 --> 00:04:16.531
Retrieval, abstention and agent behaviour

00:04:16.531 --> 00:04:17.738
retain documented limitations.

00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:21.175
Explore the code, knowledge base and

00:04:21.175 --> 00:04:22.102
fine-tuned model.

00:04:22.802 --> 00:04:24.542
Reproduce offline or connect an endpoint.

00:04:25.322 --> 00:04:25.849
Models detect.

00:04:26.482 --> 00:04:27.249
Agents coordinate.

00:04:27.615 --> 00:04:28.809
Code enforces safeguards.

00:04:29.215 --> 00:04:29.915
Humans approve.

00:04:30.615 --> 00:04:31.115
Heal the network.

00:04:31.775 --> 00:04:32.715
Improve the rulebook.
